  "name": "pump_and_check_valve_reopen",
  "description": "A pump and its discharge check valve feed a junction that a second supply reaches through an FCV with an unreachable setpoint. The FCV's first, active solve pushes the junction above the pump's shutoff head, so the pump and check valve close together and cut off the pipe between them: verifies that both are re-tested and re-open (pump running, check valve open, FCV fully open) at the closed-form operating point.",
  "source": "closed-form: tests/reference/derivations_pumps.py::pump_and_check_valve_reopen (pump curve: scipy PchipInterpolator through the points, linear end-slope extension, affinity laws H = s^2 H0(Q/s); Darcy-Weisbach + Colebrook lines with fluids entrance_sharp and exit_normal; check-valve K from fluids K_swing_check_valve_Crane (angled); FCV fully open and ideal (design 5.3 status rules); split by scipy.optimize.fsolve)",
